Skip _gtk_module_has_mixed_deps() when running as a static binary.

g_module_open(NULL) returns NULL on musl-static (no dynamic linker, so
introspecting the running process's symbol table is impossible). The
mixed-deps check is meant to detect accidental gtk2+gtk3 coexistence in
the same process — irrelevant for a self-contained static binary —
and the NULL-pointer it returns triggers two GModule-CRITICAL warnings
through g_module_symbol/g_module_close on every gtk_init().

--- a/gtk/gtkmain.c
+++ b/gtk/gtkmain.c
@@ -643,6 +643,9 @@
     module = g_module_open (NULL, 0);
   else
     module = module_to_check;
+  /* Static build: g_module_open(NULL) returns NULL (no dynamic linker
+   * to introspect). A static binary cannot have loaded a second GTK. */
+  if (!module) return FALSE;
 
   if (g_module_symbol (module, "gtk_widget_device_is_shadowed", &func))
     result = TRUE;
